WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.859 --> 00:00:06.270
Actor Brandon Routh, who donned the red cape
and proudly wore the "S" on his chest in 2006's

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:11.160
Superman Returns, is flying back onto the
small screen for the upcoming Arrowverse crossover

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:13.659
event "Crisis on Infinite Earths."

00:00:13.659 --> 00:00:18.090
Though Routh already has an Arrowverse role,
portraying Ray Palmer, the Atom, as a regular

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:23.430
on DC's Legends of Tomorrow, he'll reprise
his role as Superman along with current Arrowverse

00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:27.830
Clark Kent-slash-Superman Tyler Hoechlin,
who plays Big Blue on Supergirl.

00:00:27.830 --> 00:00:31.390
But just how and why will he be wearing the
red, blue and yellow again?

00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:36.030
Routh's tenure as the silver-screen Superman
was short-lived; he only appeared as the Man

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:38.910
of Tomorrow in Bryan Singer's Superman Returns.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:44.329
Routh was just 24 when he auditioned, and
Singer sung his praises, likening him to iconic

00:00:44.329 --> 00:00:48.899
Superman actor Christopher Reeve and describing
him as the embodiment of the world's, quote,

00:00:48.899 --> 00:00:53.309
"collective memory of Superman" thanks to
his physical appearance and his Midwestern

00:00:53.309 --> 00:00:55.700
upbringing much like Clark Kent's own.

00:00:55.700 --> 00:01:00.190
Critics largely agreed with Singer's assessment
of Routh, praising his performance.

00:01:00.190 --> 00:01:03.510
Yet Superman Returns underperformed at the
box office.

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:07.580
Warner Bros. and Legendary Pictures decided
that the sequel they had planned wouldn't

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:09.060
happen after all.

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:13.640
When Warner Bros. announced in August 2008
that the franchise would be rebooted, Routh

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:15.400
hoped to hang on to the role.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:20.640
Even after his Superman contract expired in
2009, Routh still hoped to portray the superhero

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:21.640
again.

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:25.979
Ultimately, though, Routh wasn't asked to
return: Warner Bros. instead handed Henry

00:01:25.979 --> 00:01:30.909
Cavill the cape for Man of Steel, which he
followed with appearances in Batman v. Superman

00:01:30.909 --> 00:01:32.510
and Justice League.

00:01:32.510 --> 00:01:36.360
When Arrowverse producers rang him up, the
emotion hit him hard:

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:40.229
"I hoped maybe there'd be an opportunity sometime,
but didn't really think that actually would

00:01:40.229 --> 00:01:45.330
happen, so I kinda felt like a little kid,
very shocked and excited."

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:49.330
Sure, it was something he had hoped might
happen, but was it too late?

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:52.670
Would anyone even want to see him as the Last
Son of Krypton again?

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:56.689
And worse yet, would he somehow experience
the same disappointment he had with Superman

00:01:56.689 --> 00:01:58.079
Returns?

00:01:58.079 --> 00:02:03.450
In an interview at San Diego Comic-Con 2019,
he told Entertainment Weekly he felt a "mix

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:07.290
of feelings" when he was first approached
about appearing again as Superman.

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:09.590
But obviously, Routh accepted the offer.

00:02:09.590 --> 00:02:13.910
He said "Crisis on Infinite Earths" is his
second chance at giving the superhero a proper

00:02:13.910 --> 00:02:14.910
send-off:

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:21.420
"It's an opportunity for me to kind of say
hello and goodbye to the character in a way

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:23.830
that I didn't get to do the first time."

00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:28.870
"Crisis on Infinite Earths" will span five
episodes of the various Arrowverse shows ⁠— Supergirl,

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:33.530
Arrow, The Flash, Legends of Tomorrow, and
the new Batwoman ⁠— starting in December

00:02:33.530 --> 00:02:36.200
2019 and ending in January 2020.

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:38.900
"We shoulda done a crossover."

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:39.900
"Yeah."

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:44.120
According to Deadline, Routh and fellow Superman
Hoechlin will play versions of Superman, quote,

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:48.629
"in different time frames," suggesting that
they may not meet up on screen.

00:02:48.629 --> 00:02:52.760
But considering how the Crisis on Infinite
Earths story played out in the comics, it's

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:56.480
likely that the pair are playing Supermen
from different Earths who will work together

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:58.190
to save the universe.

00:02:58.190 --> 00:03:02.361
If that's the case, "Crisis on Infinite Earths"
will not only allow Routh the chance to say

00:03:02.361 --> 00:03:06.330
goodbye to Superman, but it will also give
him the opportunity to team up with another

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:10.819
Superman who will presumably keep the cape
flying on television for years to come.

00:03:10.819 --> 00:03:15.470
And Routh is clearly stoked about the whole
situation, writing to Hoechlin on Twitter,

00:03:15.470 --> 00:03:18.520
"So excited to share the screen with you as
Supes @tylerhoechlin!

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:19.520
So fun!

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:20.560
I'm so ready!"

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:24.390
But how will Routh's other Arrowverse character,
Ray Palmer, fit in?

00:03:24.390 --> 00:03:29.230
Chatting with IGN host Max Scoville at Comic-Con,
Routh said it'll be interesting if he gets

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:33.349
to play both the Atom and Superman for "Crisis
on Infinite Earths," because they're such

00:03:33.349 --> 00:03:34.540
similar characters.

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:37.410
"Ray is kind of modeled a little bit after
Clark.

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:40.670
There are definitely Clark...Clark energy
in Ray.

00:03:40.670 --> 00:03:45.370
Um, so I'd say, you know, there's a fair bit
of crossover."

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:49.620
See Routh finally return as Superman when
the "Crisis on Infinite Earths" event beings

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:51.870
this December on the CW.

